Audio is three decisions, not one list
=====================================

The Audio tab was a device list with two model selects bolted on. Listening, speaking and holding a
conversation are three different decisions, so they are three sections now, each saying what it is,
what this build runs underneath, and what the alternative costs.

  * **Speech to text** — input device and engine. Whisper on this machine by default: a few seconds per
    clip, the audio never leaves the box. Cloud sends the recording to a provider. Off is a real
    choice and it is in the list.
  * **Text to speech** — output device, engine, voice. Kokoro on this machine by default; the voice is
    a name rather than a preset list, because the voices are files.
  * **Conversation** — both at once, with the mode spelled out: *off / push to talk / always listening*.
    Push-to-talk is the default because a microphone that opens itself is a decision, not a
    convenience, and choosing always-listening shows the warning that an open microphone is a real
    thing rather than a setting. The push-to-talk key lives here too, where it belongs.

The footer line reads the live services — `voice ready (kokoro) · transcription ready (whisper)` or the
truth about what is not running — from `/api/quixi/voice/status`, so "under the skin" is a reading
rather than a promise.

Also in this patch, the About Nora text: **"built by a person with a disability."** No diagnosis in the
intro. Asked what disability, the persona may say that he is disabled and that he does not like to
talk about it — and then stop.

